It certainly depends on role. As we are talking here of Samurai:
Martial arts, Two-weapon combat, long sword and clerical spells add
to 22 (if I recall correctly). If I go for riding another 4 slots
are used up. The remaining I usually split between attack spells 
and some throwing weapon which can be used while still two-weaponing:
  Shuriken - if I find enough (shops, polypiling - depends on the
     aimed-for conduct)
  Dagger (seldom as they are heavy) - usually if I come across Sting,
     Ocrist or a decent athame early in game
  Darts - the most common situation
Keep in mind that you have only 29 slots at maximum! The first 22 I
think mandatory for Samurai. If you don't use some steed (I often
don't) you are a bit more free. Nevertheless: bow and saber are not
the best choices, IMHO.

